msgctxt "Addon Summary"
msgid "Automatically switch Kodi to software decoding by video type or per TV show, or to fix known hardware decoder issues."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "Addon Description"
msgid "Hardware decoding is usually preferred, but sometimes it gets things wrong, or there are known issues.  Manually changing settings is a chore, so Limp aims to make that easier by automatically engaging software decoding when you need or want it, and automatically switching back when done.\n\nYou can choose when software decoding engages:\n\n* for video types known to trip up the hardware decoder (Amlogic/CoreELEC)\n* automatically, for all videos 1080p and below\n* for any single video, from the context menu\n* for specific TV shows you choose (via the context menu)\n\nCurrently works on Amlogic (CoreELEC and derivatives), Windows, Apple devices and webOS.  If you need other platforms, please create a GitHub issue to discuss."
msgstr ""

